
<p>Michael Acton, reporting for the Financial Times from San Francisco:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>About 40 former employees now working at OpenAI have been sent
letters directing them to preserve documents and communications
and demanding meetings with Apple’s lawyers, according to multiple
people familiar with the matter. Apple and OpenAI declined to
comment.</p>

<p>The decision to hit employees with personal legal letters
highlights Apple’s aggressive tactics after it last week launched
a blockbuster lawsuit accusing OpenAI and two employees of
stealing secret hardware plans.</p>
</blockquote>

